  "content": {
    "id": "p40-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Two trains each make a journey of 330 km.\n\nOne of the trains travels 5 km/h faster than the other and takes 30 minutes less time.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p40-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that this scenario can be modelled using the equation $\\dfrac{330}{v}-\\dfrac{330}{v+5}=\\dfrac{1}{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Let $v>0$ be the slower train's speed in km/h. Journey times are $\\dfrac{330}{v}$ and $\\dfrac{330}{v+5}$ hours, so $\\dfrac{330}{v}-\\dfrac{330}{v+5}=\\dfrac12$.",
          "worked": "Let $v>0$ be the slower train's speed in km/h. The faster train's speed is $(v+5)$ km/h. Using time = distance ÷ speed:\n$$\\begin{align*}t_{\\text{slower}}&=\\frac{330}{v}\\text{ h}\\\\t_{\\text{faster}}&=\\frac{330}{v+5}\\text{ h}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe faster train takes 30 minutes, or $\\frac12$ hour, less time. Hence\n$$\\frac{330}{v}-\\frac{330}{v+5}=\\frac12.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p40-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence find the speeds of the trains.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "55 km/h and 60 km/h. Solve $v^2+5v-3300=0$ and reject the negative speed.",
          "worked": "Since $v>0$, multiply by $2v(v+5)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}660(v+5)-660v&=v(v+5)\\\\3300&=v^2+5v\\\\v^2+5v-3300&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $a=1$, $b=5$ and $c=-3300$. Using the quadratic formula:\n$$\\begin{align*}v&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{5^2-4(1)(-3300)}}{2(1)}\\\\v&=\\frac{-5\\pm\\sqrt{13225}}{2}\\\\v&=\\frac{-5\\pm115}{2}\\\\v&=55\\text{ or }-60.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $v=-60$ because a speed must be positive. The speeds are $55$ km/h and $55+5=60$ km/h.\n\nCheck: $330\\div55=6$ hours and $330\\div60=5.5$ hours, a difference of 30 minutes.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
